Q: Store session data using MemoryStore in Node, similar to $_SESSION[&#39;data&#39;] = value in PHP A: <p>This worked for me - you basically just have to set a key in the sessionStore:</p>

<pre><code>io.sockets.on('connection', function (socket) {
     socket.on('details', function(data){
          console.log("Details: " + data.u + data.p);
          if(data.p == "admin" &amp;&amp; data.u == "admin")
          {
               // set the value
               sessionStore.loggedIn = true;
               // get the value
               console.log(sessionStore.loggedIn);
          }
     });
});
</code></pre>

<p>I tried it on a website with some subpages, the value was consistent. A forced reload or closing the browser resets it.</p>

Q: Angular onChange programmatically triggered does not work A: <p>The issue is here:</p>
<pre><code>(change)=&quot;onChange&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>It should be:</p>
<pre><code>(change)=&quot;onChange($event)&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>In your child component, add an output:</p>
<pre><code>@Output() change = new EventEmitter&lt;any&gt;();
</code></pre>
<p>Then emit it manually when value changes:</p>
<pre><code>onInputChange() {
  this.onChange(this.data);
  this.change.emit(this.data);
}

onClick() {
  this.data = 'clicked';
  this.onChange(this.data);
  this.change.emit(this.data);
}
</code></pre>
<p>Parent:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;mycomponent
  [(ngModel)]=&quot;mydata&quot;
  (change)=&quot;onChange($event)&quot;
&gt;
&lt;/mycomponent&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Xaml StringFormat and static strings A: <p>You can decompose your <code>TextBlock</code> in multiple <code>Run</code> elements:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;TextBlock&gt;
    &lt;Run Text=&quot;Started&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;Run Text=&quot;{Binding MyDate, StringFormat={x:Static i:Format.DateTime}}&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/TexBlock&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Note: a space is automatically added between the <code>Run</code> elements when they are placed on different lines.</p>
